{title: This Is The Prayer That I Pray}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
Has the time really gone by so quickly?
Seems in no time at all we have grown.
You have always been there as my brother,
With the care and the kindness you've shown.
Now today, you step out toward the future
With the gift of the Lord by your side,
With the blessing of all who have gathered
To rejoice as you stand with your bride.

Chorus
May you together
Grow stronger each day in your love,
Sharing forever
The grace of our Father above.
May He shower His blessings upon you,
As you live for His glory each day.
May he comfort and guide you, my brother:
This is the prayer that I pray.

Verse 2
(2nd verse)
I am glad I can share in this moment,
As we've shared in so many before.
Now you've found love that lasts for a lifetime,
As together you walk through the door.
I am glad that as onward we travel,
The road that we share does not end.
For I am not losing a brother:
I am gaining a sister and friend!

Ending
May He comfort and guide you,
My brother, my sister...
This is the prayer that I pray.
